==Enemy==
When the Aku Altar is around, be ready for a tough battle, as its mere presence puts a handicap on all [[Cat Units]]' levels depending on how much progress has been made in [[The Aku Realms]] as well as cancelling out + levels (see the linked article for more information) until the [[Mount Aku (Aku Realm)/Invasion|Mount Aku Invasion]] has been cleared, at which point it turns into an [[Inactive Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Inactive Aku Altar]] and loses its effects. On its own, however, it does absolutely nothing to harm your units. As the name suggests, it always appears with [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku enemies]].

==Strategy==
Due to this base's effect, what ends up mattering in its presence is units' stats when not skewed by + levels, meaning that [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]], who often have more + levels than normal ones (20+90 being the max), end up massively underpowered, to the point of becoming useless. Similarly, [[:Category:Li'l Cats|Li'l Cats]] and [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cats]] tend to rely on + levels more than [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rares]], who tend to rely more on them than [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] and no-gacha Cats. This results in cats of high rarity as well as drop rewards having a general advantage and being, therefore, recommended to use with priority (note that low priority doesn't mean anyone should be put on the side-lines, sometimes, if not often, stat-based Rares are still more than viable). However, units such as crowd controllers are affected far less, as these units don't usually rely on their stats.

Aside from altering the unit balance, this base also has somewhat of an equalizing effect, allowing underleveled units to be used alongside high-level ones when the level cap is low.

[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]] and [[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units can deal some extra damage to it using their abilities, due to it not having any Immunity to them.

